  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66850,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyalinizing clear cell carcinomas are endobronchial in central airways.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:03:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66851,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The central location predominantly causes symptoms of obstruction, cough, and dyspnoea. Haemoptysis is rare {31343850}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:03:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66852,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyalinizing clear cell carcinomas are rare lung cancers, with only 11&nbsp;reported cases. The age range is 30&ndash;66&nbsp;years, with a slight female predominance {28927164; 30429005; 26645458; 25545688}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:03:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66853,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:03:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66854,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:03:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66855,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "<p>Hyalinizing clear cell carcinomas are tan-white, relatively circumscribed, unencapsulated tumours. Invasion into bronchial cartilage can occur {25545688}. Sizes range from 9 to 35 mm {26645458; 29434341}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-02T10:54:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66856,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyalinizing clear cell carcinomas are composed of small to medium-sized cells with clear or pale eosinophilic cytoplasm infiltrating in cords, nests, and trabeculae. The cells infiltrate within a background of alternating myxohyaline and fibrous stroma. Mitotic activity is minimal and necrosis is not seen. Occasional cells have intracytoplasmic mucin. Perineural invasion can be present, and peritumoural lymphocytic infiltrations are seen {26645458; 25543160; 28508996; 25545688; 29434341}. Tumour cells are positive for CK7, high-molecular-weight cytokeratin (34&beta;E12), CK5/6, p63, and p40. Positivity for EMA, CAM5.2, CK19, and CK14 has been reported {26645458}. Tumour cells are negative for TTF1, napsin&nbsp;A, CK20, S100, SMA, synaptophysin, and chromogranin {25545688; 29434341}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:03:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66857,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumour cells are small to medium-sized, with either clear or pale eosinophilic cytoplasm; they are present as loose clusters and single cells with round uniform nuclei, small prominent nucleoli, and abundant wispy cytoplasm {31343850}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:03:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66858,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The <em>EWSR1</em>-<em>ATF1</em> fusion is present in all reported cases {29434341}. One case reports an <em>EWSR1</em>-<em>CREM</em> fusion by FISH, which is also found in head and neck primaries {29975250}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:03:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66859,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Low-grade epithelial cells with variable areas of cells with clear cytoplasm and cells with eosinophilic cytoplasm, within myxohyaline and sclerotic stroma</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Demonstration of <em>EWSR1</em>-<em>ATF1</em> fusion</li>\r\n</ul>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-04T10:08:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66860,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "<p>Staging is according to the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM classification.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-18T17:04:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66861,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyalinizing clear cell carcinomas are low-grade, with an indolent course. No recurrences have been reported after resection {25543160; 28508996}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:03:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]